A||||5||-=shame=-||Under coating ?||||5||
Z||000000||-=shame=-||09-12-2000||07:33 AM||||Has anyone ever undercoated their Fiero, or had to work on one that has been coated? I'm planing on powerwashing and undercoating mine this weekend but would like to know if there is anything specific I should avoid getting that crap on. Plus any tips on how to maybe wrap-up the radiator 'hoses' that run along the sides.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stsmithgt||09-12-2000||11:35 AM||||It may sound a little redneck and it may be a little messy BUT, if you use duct tape to cover what you don't want undercoated sounds like it would work.  If it's peeled off before the undercoating has hardened up I think it would work.  If the tape is too strong(sticky) where you think it might be too hard to get off, you can "kill" it like at a bodyshop. Stick it to something else first like your pant leg to weaken the adheasion of the tape.  I've done it with masking tape, but I think masking tape would be too weak with the undercoating application.  It doesn't seem like there's too much to undercoat on a Fiero since there's so much plastic where undercoat would usually go.?<BR>Well hows that for 2 cents worth of an IDEA?||||reg||3
Z||000002||theogre||09-12-2000||11:47 AM||||Undercoating isn't worth bothering with unless you get rid of all the rust first. Another thing to consider is that if any rust is inside things like frame rails undercoating won't help and could hide it when it eats thru the rail.<P>You'll also need to let the car dry for a day or 3 after washing. If not you'll trap water in things and/or you won't get a good bond.<P>You want to keep it off any bolt that may need service. If you get it on the head its annoying but the threads.....<P>Just use big masking tape. You can get it 2inches or more wide.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-12-2000||05:26 PM||||You would be better off using paint because that undercoating stuff can trap water between the metal and the undercoating and cause some rust damage to your fiero. Use Rust-oleum Rusty Metal primer and a coat of flat black paint. If you have any rust under your car than remove as much of it as you can with a wire brush and neutralize the remaining rust with that stuff that turns rust into black primer.||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||09-12-2000||05:45 PM||||Rust converter!  Creates an oxidation which is why the rust turns black.<P>Hit your drain holes directly under the seats and any other cancer going on under there.  paint some black rust-o over it to protect.  Don't forget the trunk area in the corners.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">   <BR>   <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000005||-=shame=-||09-12-2000||06:20 PM||||Sounds great fellas, but I think it's worth it, not necessarily for rust but road noise. So here's the plan; wash it, Rust-o it, undercoat it.||||reg||1
